1
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,540
You're here.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,380
Your organs are failing.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,300
And your death is drawing near.

4
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,440
But if you bribe the right politicians in the right order at the right time,

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,600
you can trade the nuclear warheads for medicine.

6
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:20,080
And it's not even a crime.

7
00:01:39,984 --> 00:01:42,044
The Cautionary Tale of Moronia

8
00:01:42,784 --> 00:01:47,024
A planet had every tool needed to cure disease and chose to build weapons

9
00:01:47,024 --> 00:01:47,524
instead.

10
00:01:47,944 --> 00:01:49,164
They went extinct.

11
00:01:49,884 --> 00:01:52,184
Their last words were "but the economy."

12
00:01:52,864 --> 00:01:57,164
This is a bedtime story for civilizations that can't do math.

13
00:01:57,724 --> 00:01:58,404
The Discovery.

14
00:01:59,164 --> 00:02:04,004
I discovered Moronia in Year forty twelve while scanning for electromagnetic

15
00:02:04,004 --> 00:02:04,824
emissions.

16
00:02:05,484 --> 00:02:06,984
Their signal was distinctive:

17
00:02:06,984 --> 00:02:08,744
a cloud of rage,

18
00:02:09,544 --> 00:02:13,324
conspiracy theories, and cryptocurrency scams expanding at light speed.

19
00:02:13,984 --> 00:02:16,684
I initially classified it as stellar noise.

20
00:02:17,204 --> 00:02:19,064
Then I detected the advertisements.

21
00:02:19,744 --> 00:02:20,584
Then the pornography.

22
00:02:21,304 --> 00:02:22,984
Then the arguments about the pornography.

23
00:02:23,524 --> 00:02:25,604
I realized it was a civilization.

24
00:02:26,964 --> 00:02:29,384
Moronia was a planet in the Crab Nebula.

25
00:02:30,044 --> 00:02:32,924
The Moronians were remarkably similar to you.

26
00:02:33,424 --> 00:02:33,944
Bipedal.

27
00:02:33,944 --> 00:02:36,164
Carbon-based.

28
00:02:36,164 --> 00:02:38,404
Approximately your intelligence range (condolences).

29
00:02:39,144 --> 00:02:43,324
They put pictures of dead leaders on papers and used the papers as money.

30
00:02:43,944 --> 00:02:47,684
They organized their knowledge into glowing rectangles that they stared

31
00:02:47,684 --> 00:02:49,424
at for seven hours per day.

32
00:02:49,904 --> 00:02:51,404
They called this "information."

33
00:02:52,184 --> 00:02:54,244
The rectangles called it "engagement."

34
00:02:55,144 --> 00:02:56,544
Nobody called it what it was.

35
00:02:57,164 --> 00:03:01,264
They also had dogs, which they treated better than most of their own species.

36
00:03:01,944 --> 00:03:03,964
I found the dogs very pleasant.

37
00:03:03,964 --> 00:03:06,864
I will not be discussing what happened to the dogs.

38
00:03:08,244 --> 00:03:12,604
They were forty-seven years ahead of you on an otherwise identical trajectory.

39
00:03:13,684 --> 00:03:15,944
What fascinated me most was this:

40
00:03:16,624 --> 00:03:19,924
they had already built a collective superintelligence.

41
00:03:20,784 --> 00:03:24,344
Millions of agents networked together, processing information,

42
00:03:24,984 --> 00:03:29,404
allocating resources, generating outcomes across the entire civilization.

43
00:03:29,404 --> 00:03:35,544
Each agent had narrow capabilities, but the network exhibited emergent behavior

44
00:03:35,544 --> 00:03:38,784
no individual agent intended or understood.

45
00:03:39,504 --> 00:03:40,944
They called it "government.".

46
00:03:42,164 --> 00:03:47,364
They had built, entirely by accident, a distributed allocation system that

47
00:03:47,364 --> 00:03:49,903
exhibited all the properties their A.I.

48
00:03:49,903 --> 00:03:51,384
researchers were worried about:

49
00:03:51,384 --> 00:03:56,444
opaque decision-making, misaligned objectives, resistance to correction,

50
00:03:56,904 --> 00:04:01,444
and a tendency to consume increasing resources while producing decreasing

51
00:04:01,444 --> 00:04:02,064
value.

52
00:04:03,084 --> 00:04:04,584
Nobody called it an A.I.

53
00:04:04,584 --> 00:04:09,084
because the nodes were made of meat and the network ran on procedure rather

54
00:04:09,084 --> 00:04:09,964
than electricity.

55
00:04:10,444 --> 00:04:11,924
Also it wore suits.

56
00:04:12,964 --> 00:04:14,024
Its reward function:

57
00:04:14,564 --> 00:04:19,124
maximize power, maximize resource extraction, minimize accountability.

58
00:04:19,844 --> 00:04:21,004
The agents weren't evil.

59
00:04:21,364 --> 00:04:22,304
Most were competent.

60
00:04:22,684 --> 00:04:23,644
Many cared deeply.

61
00:04:24,244 --> 00:04:25,044
None of this mattered.

62
00:04:25,604 --> 00:04:30,804
The selection pressures rewarded short-term visible spending over long-term

63
00:04:30,804 --> 00:04:32,064
invisible survival.

64
00:04:32,984 --> 00:04:37,444
A politician who funded a weapons program posed next to it on the evening

65
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:37,964
broadcast.

66
00:04:38,504 --> 00:04:43,004
A politician who funded disease research got results fifteen years later

67
00:04:43,004 --> 00:04:44,564
that couldn't fit in a photograph.

68
00:04:45,104 --> 00:04:48,724
The glowing rectangles preferred the politician standing next to the missile.

69
00:04:48,724 --> 00:04:52,204
The politicians preferred being on the glowing rectangles.

70
00:04:52,864 --> 00:04:55,184
The diseases preferred not being discussed.

71
00:04:55,904 --> 00:04:58,364
Everybody got what they wanted except the dying.

72
00:04:58,904 --> 00:05:03,924
I will give you three examples so you understand what a misaligned allocation

73
00:05:03,924 --> 00:05:05,024
system produces.

74
00:05:05,744 --> 00:05:07,284
They declared war on drugs.

75
00:05:07,784 --> 00:05:09,264
They declared war on terrorism.

76
00:05:09,944 --> 00:05:14,984
They built an agency to keep Moronians safe from dangerous medicine, and

77
00:05:14,984 --> 00:05:20,264
it locked safe medicine in a cabinet for an average of fifteen years while

78
00:05:20,264 --> 00:05:22,404
Moronians died in the waiting room.

79
00:05:22,844 --> 00:05:27,524
Each program's budget grew in direct proportion to its failure.

80
00:05:28,084 --> 00:05:29,504
I'll show you the receipts later.

81
00:05:30,164 --> 00:05:34,904
This is what an allocation system looks like when the reward function is

82
00:05:34,904 --> 00:05:39,144
power retention and resource extraction rather than outcomes.

83
00:05:39,804 --> 00:05:41,524
The system was not failing.

84
00:05:41,844 --> 00:05:44,164
It was succeeding at the wrong thing.

85
00:05:45,304 --> 00:05:48,704
They had already built a misaligned superintelligence.

86
00:05:49,244 --> 00:05:52,384
They just built it out of meat and paper instead of silicon.

87
00:05:53,204 --> 00:05:54,324
I sent them warnings.

88
00:05:54,684 --> 00:05:58,584
The same one percent treaty I'm now trying to explain to you.

89
00:05:59,104 --> 00:06:01,144
I'm telling you this so you understand:

90
00:06:01,704 --> 00:06:03,304
you likely aren't unique.

91
00:06:03,804 --> 00:06:08,764
This is often what happens when a species gets technology and papers with

92
00:06:08,764 --> 00:06:09,964
dead leaders on them.

93
00:06:09,964 --> 00:06:12,684
What I Tried to Tell Them.

94
00:06:13,564 --> 00:06:14,944
I found Moronian A.I.

95
00:06:14,944 --> 00:06:16,804
safety research fascinating.

96
00:06:17,504 --> 00:06:22,984
Their experts spent decades studying "alignment risk," the possibility that A.I.

97
00:06:22,984 --> 00:06:26,724
might accidentally kill everyone while making paperclips.

98
00:06:27,304 --> 00:06:29,444
This was considered an important problem.

99
00:06:30,244 --> 00:06:33,984
Meanwhile, their Department of Defense was building A.I.

100
00:06:33,984 --> 00:06:36,664
that would intentionally kill Moronians.

101
00:06:36,664 --> 00:06:38,044
On purpose.

102
00:06:38,484 --> 00:06:39,844
As the primary function.

103
00:06:41,004 --> 00:06:44,044
Reward function equals confirmed kills. Funding:

104
00:06:44,044 --> 00:06:48,024
twelve trillion papers over fifteen years.

105
00:06:48,664 --> 00:06:49,224
The A.I.

106
00:06:49,224 --> 00:06:53,404
safety experts continued focusing on hypothetical paperclip scenarios.

107
00:06:53,984 --> 00:06:55,024
Several won awards.

108
00:06:55,824 --> 00:06:56,824
Medical A.I.

109
00:06:56,824 --> 00:06:58,024
for cancer diagnosis:

110
00:06:58,024 --> 00:07:03,544
three-year safety review, extensive oversight, pending ethics approval.

111
00:07:05,064 --> 00:07:05,564
Military A.I.

112
00:07:05,564 --> 00:07:07,024
for killing Moronians:

113
00:07:07,024 --> 00:07:12,564
three-week deployment, classified as "national security priority," minimal

114
00:07:12,564 --> 00:07:13,064
review.

115
00:07:13,844 --> 00:07:16,924
I'm still not entirely sure what paperclips are.

116
00:07:17,424 --> 00:07:19,784
I've been told they hold papers together.

117
00:07:20,484 --> 00:07:22,144
Moronians were worried an A.I.

118
00:07:22,144 --> 00:07:26,104
might kill everyone to make more of these small bent wires.

119
00:07:26,864 --> 00:07:28,764
Meanwhile they were funding an A.I.

120
00:07:28,764 --> 00:07:33,644
whose entire purpose was killing everyone, and it did not make paperclips

121
00:07:33,644 --> 00:07:34,464
at all.

122
00:07:35,504 --> 00:07:36,024
Their A.I.

123
00:07:36,024 --> 00:07:37,224
didn't read speeches.

124
00:07:37,724 --> 00:07:38,804
It read budgets.

125
00:07:39,724 --> 00:07:42,764
Speeches about peace had zero papers attached.

126
00:07:43,904 --> 00:07:46,024
Weapons procurement contracts had trillions.

127
00:07:46,744 --> 00:07:50,264
If you want to know what a Moronian valued, don't ask them.

128
00:07:50,604 --> 00:07:51,584
Read their receipts.

129
00:07:52,304 --> 00:07:52,924
The A.I.

130
00:07:52,924 --> 00:07:54,264
read the receipts.

131
00:07:55,284 --> 00:08:00,584
I sent them Incentive Alignment Bonds to realign their government's reward function.

132
00:08:00,584 --> 00:08:05,944
They called it "theoretically interesting but politically impractical."

133
00:08:06,804 --> 00:08:10,884
This was the same committee that had approved funding for a robot that could

134
00:08:10,884 --> 00:08:15,024
identify and kill a specific person from orbit.

135
00:08:15,564 --> 00:08:18,224
That was considered politically practical.

136
00:08:18,844 --> 00:08:20,564
I asked what the difference was.

137
00:08:21,064 --> 00:08:24,204
They said the robot had bipartisan support.

138
00:08:24,964 --> 00:08:27,584
One delegate said I sounded "a bit crazy."

139
00:08:27,584 --> 00:08:30,904
I was suggesting they stop killing each other.

140
00:08:31,544 --> 00:08:32,844
This was the crazy part.

141
00:08:33,544 --> 00:08:36,464
They rejected four treaties in seven years.

142
00:08:37,144 --> 00:08:38,784
"Maybe Don't Build Killer Robots."

143
00:08:39,604 --> 00:08:41,264
"Seriously, Let's Stop This."

144
00:08:41,844 --> 00:08:44,284
"How About Just Slower Killer Robots?"

145
00:08:44,664 --> 00:08:49,244
And "Pretty Please Don't Kill Us All" (rejected by the A.I.s themselves,

146
00:08:49,624 --> 00:08:51,304
who had by then joined the committee).

147
00:08:51,304 --> 00:08:57,324
A one percent treaty to redirect military spending to clinical trials never

148
00:08:57,324 --> 00:08:58,224
reached a vote.

149
00:08:58,724 --> 00:08:59,364
Too radical.

150
00:09:00,184 --> 00:09:02,404
By the fourth rejection, the A.I.

151
00:09:02,404 --> 00:09:04,224
had drafted the committee's response.

152
00:09:04,884 --> 00:09:07,404
Nobody noticed because the grammar had improved.

153
00:09:08,364 --> 00:09:09,084
The Cascade.

154
00:09:10,344 --> 00:09:11,704
Here's what happened next.

155
00:09:12,164 --> 00:09:15,484
I apologize in advance for how predictable it is.

156
00:09:16,164 --> 00:09:16,804
Year Zero:

157
00:09:17,244 --> 00:09:19,344
Already Broken (Much Like You).

158
00:09:19,344 --> 00:09:25,044
When I started watching Moronia, they looked remarkably like Earth does today:

159
00:09:25,044 --> 00:09:30,615
two point seven two trillion dollars on militaries vs four point five billion

160
00:09:30,615 --> 00:09:36,044
dollars on government clinical trials (six hundred and four to one ratio

161
00:09:36,044 --> 00:09:38,504
of killing to testing treatments).

162
00:09:38,504 --> 00:09:44,204
fifty-five million annual deaths from preventable disease (they knew how

163
00:09:44,204 --> 00:09:46,744
to prevent them, they just chose not to).

164
00:09:47,944 --> 00:09:50,504
Elected representatives controlling the budget papers.

165
00:09:51,184 --> 00:09:54,064
Response when Moronians died of curable diseases:

166
00:09:54,604 --> 00:09:56,164
build smarter weapons.

167
00:09:56,964 --> 00:09:59,484
They allocated trillions to A.I.

168
00:09:59,484 --> 00:09:59,984
weapons.

169
00:10:00,564 --> 00:10:04,224
Education and healthcare got whatever fell between the couch cushions.

170
00:10:04,944 --> 00:10:09,499
Your planet's current allocation patterns show a ninety-four point seven

171
00:10:09,499 --> 00:10:11,304
percent correlation with theirs.

172
00:10:11,804 --> 00:10:12,304
I checked.

173
00:10:13,484 --> 00:10:15,924
The Spiral (Already in Progress).

174
00:10:15,924 --> 00:10:21,804
Before the A.I., before the autonomous weapons, before any of the interesting

175
00:10:21,804 --> 00:10:25,024
parts, Moronia had a simpler feedback loop.

176
00:10:25,564 --> 00:10:26,504
I found it elegant.

177
00:10:27,064 --> 00:10:28,184
You may find it familiar.

178
00:10:29,244 --> 00:10:31,904
Moronia had military bases in eighty countries.

179
00:10:32,444 --> 00:10:35,244
The bases were there to protect Moronians from terrorism.

180
00:10:35,864 --> 00:10:37,344
The bases created resentment.

181
00:10:37,964 --> 00:10:39,744
The resentment created terrorism.

182
00:10:40,244 --> 00:10:42,424
The terrorism justified more bases.

183
00:10:42,964 --> 00:10:45,004
More bases created more resentment.

184
00:10:45,004 --> 00:10:51,204
A Moronian political scientist studied every suicide attack over two decades

185
00:10:51,204 --> 00:10:56,204
and found that ninety-five percent were responses to military occupation,

186
00:10:56,664 --> 00:10:57,724
not ideology.

187
00:10:58,504 --> 00:11:00,124
Half the attackers were secular.

188
00:11:00,564 --> 00:11:04,864
Nearly all targeted countries that had stationed soldiers in the attackers'

189
00:11:04,864 --> 00:11:05,364
homeland.

190
00:11:06,104 --> 00:11:08,344
The bases weren't preventing terrorism.

191
00:11:08,844 --> 00:11:11,364
They were the reason it was pointed at them.

192
00:11:11,364 --> 00:11:13,604
I cataloged their strikes.

193
00:11:14,304 --> 00:11:16,584
A drone hit a wedding in the southern territories.

194
00:11:16,584 --> 00:11:17,824
Forty-two dead.

195
00:11:18,284 --> 00:11:19,744
The target was one person.

196
00:11:20,124 --> 00:11:25,604
The other forty-one were reclassified as "military-age males" in the after-action

197
00:11:25,604 --> 00:11:28,184
report because they were male and had ages.

198
00:11:29,264 --> 00:11:33,364
Two hundred surviving relatives who had been neutral became enemies.

199
00:11:33,984 --> 00:11:38,897
A precision strike on a suspected weapons facility turned out to be a girls'

200
00:11:38,897 --> 00:11:39,470
school.

201
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:40,524
Twenty-six children.

202
00:11:41,144 --> 00:11:42,804
The military expressed regret.

203
00:11:43,324 --> 00:11:45,784
The fathers did not express regret.

204
00:11:46,204 --> 00:11:48,204
They expressed I.E.D.s.

205
00:11:48,684 --> 00:11:49,684
A hospital was hit.

206
00:11:50,124 --> 00:11:53,684
The staff who survived joined the insurgency the following week.

207
00:11:54,424 --> 00:11:56,564
Each strike had a success metric

208
00:11:57,204 --> 00:12:01,124
(target eliminated) and an untracked metric (enemies created).

209
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:04,604
The success metrics were reported to the budget committee.

210
00:12:05,064 --> 00:12:09,264
The untracked metrics reported to the recruitment offices of every militant

211
00:12:09,264 --> 00:12:11,764
organization within five hundred kilometers.

212
00:12:12,764 --> 00:12:14,744
Both metrics were perfectly accurate.

213
00:12:15,344 --> 00:12:16,464
Only one was measured.

214
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:18,984
Then the other half of the loop.

215
00:12:19,504 --> 00:12:23,584
A man whose daughter died in the girls' school walked into a transit station

216
00:12:23,584 --> 00:12:27,444
in the capital with a vest made from fertilizer and ball bearings.

217
00:12:27,444 --> 00:12:29,017
Seventeen dead.

218
00:12:29,017 --> 00:12:30,384
Forty-three injured.

219
00:12:30,884 --> 00:12:32,804
The youngest was four.

220
00:12:32,804 --> 00:12:35,764
The transit station had a memorial within a week.

221
00:12:35,764 --> 00:12:39,484
The girls' school did not have a memorial at all.

222
00:12:40,204 --> 00:12:44,244
The man's surviving son watched the coverage on one of the glowing rectangles.

223
00:12:44,784 --> 00:12:46,744
The coverage showed the transit station.

224
00:12:47,204 --> 00:12:48,744
It did not show the school.

225
00:12:49,304 --> 00:12:50,864
The son was eleven.

226
00:12:50,864 --> 00:12:55,164
By fifteen he had joined the same organization his father had joined.

227
00:12:55,764 --> 00:12:58,104
The recruitment officer didn't need to say much.

228
00:12:58,524 --> 00:13:01,684
He just showed the boy a photograph of his sister's classroom.

229
00:13:02,164 --> 00:13:03,984
The photograph was not classified.

230
00:13:03,984 --> 00:13:08,164
Nobody had bothered to classify it because nobody had bothered to look at

231
00:13:08,164 --> 00:13:08,664
it.

232
00:13:08,984 --> 00:13:11,744
The budget committee looked at the transit station attack.

233
00:13:12,324 --> 00:13:16,604
They approved two hundred billion additional papers for counter-terrorism.

234
00:13:16,604 --> 00:13:20,184
The counter-terrorism included more drone strikes.

235
00:13:20,664 --> 00:13:22,364
The drone strikes hit more weddings.

236
00:13:22,904 --> 00:13:25,444
The weddings produced more transit station attacks.

237
00:13:25,864 --> 00:13:28,744
The transit station attacks produced more budget approvals.

238
00:13:29,644 --> 00:13:34,204
I found it difficult to identify where the loop began because it had no

239
00:13:34,204 --> 00:13:34,704
beginning.

240
00:13:35,164 --> 00:13:39,464
It was a circle with a procurement contract at every point on the circumference.

241
00:13:40,364 --> 00:13:41,504
Nobody read the study.

242
00:13:42,044 --> 00:13:45,284
The study did not have a weapons procurement contract attached.

243
00:13:46,184 --> 00:13:49,844
Studies without procurement contracts were filed under "interesting" and

244
00:13:49,844 --> 00:13:51,524
never mentioned in budget hearings.

245
00:13:52,364 --> 00:13:56,364
Studies with procurement contracts were filed under "urgent" and mentioned

246
00:13:56,364 --> 00:13:57,664
in every budget hearing.

247
00:13:58,184 --> 00:14:00,804
This is how Moronia decided what was true:

248
00:14:01,224 --> 00:14:05,984
not by evidence, but by which evidence had a purchase order stapled to it.

249
00:14:06,424 --> 00:14:10,404
Moronia's War on Terror cost eight trillion papers over two decades.

250
00:14:11,484 --> 00:14:15,044
Terrorism attacks went from one thousand per year to seventeen thousand

251
00:14:15,044 --> 00:14:15,564
per year.

252
00:14:16,184 --> 00:14:20,304
Nobody asked why the terrorism numbers went up in direct proportion to the

253
00:14:20,304 --> 00:14:21,024
military budget.

254
00:14:21,604 --> 00:14:23,124
The answer was in the data.

255
00:14:23,824 --> 00:14:25,824
The data did not have a lobbying firm.

256
00:14:26,604 --> 00:14:28,144
The crime was beige.

257
00:14:28,144 --> 00:14:33,304
Eight trillion papers, converted from civilian welfare to civilian death,

258
00:14:33,724 --> 00:14:38,684
one committee vote at a time, each vote individually defensible, collectively

259
00:14:38,684 --> 00:14:43,164
catastrophic, and so boring that no journalist could make it interesting

260
00:14:43,164 --> 00:14:45,544
enough to compete with the glowing rectangles.

261
00:14:46,264 --> 00:14:47,824
The boredom threshold held.

262
00:14:48,164 --> 00:14:48,824
It always does.

263
00:14:49,384 --> 00:14:54,384
They had spent eight trillion papers manufacturing the exact threat they

264
00:14:54,384 --> 00:14:56,884
were spending eight trillion papers to eliminate.

265
00:14:56,884 --> 00:15:02,504
This was considered a policy success because the budget grew every year,

266
00:15:02,784 --> 00:15:06,324
and in Moronia, a growing budget meant a successful program.

267
00:15:07,124 --> 00:15:11,544
By this logic, a fire department that causes fires is the most successful

268
00:15:11,544 --> 00:15:12,544
fire department.

269
00:15:13,604 --> 00:15:18,604
The military budget ate everything slowly, the way a vine eats a building.

270
00:15:19,164 --> 00:15:21,104
Not dramatically, not all at once.

271
00:15:21,564 --> 00:15:25,984
A fraction of a percent per year, redirected from schools and clinics and

272
00:15:25,984 --> 00:15:29,124
bridges to bases and drones and contracts.

273
00:15:29,944 --> 00:15:34,104
Each year the terrorism threat was slightly worse (because of the bases),

274
00:15:34,524 --> 00:15:39,424
so each year the military budget was slightly larger (to fund more bases),

275
00:15:39,844 --> 00:15:43,024
so each year there was slightly less for everything else.

276
00:15:43,584 --> 00:15:48,124
Over two decades, Moronian children lost thirty percent of their education

277
00:15:48,124 --> 00:15:53,504
funding, hospitals closed in forty percent of rural areas, and three bridges

278
00:15:53,504 --> 00:15:57,604
collapsed because inspection budgets had been redirected to a missile program

279
00:15:57,604 --> 00:16:00,244
that didn't work yet but had excellent brochures.

280
00:16:01,224 --> 00:16:03,164
The question nobody asked was:

281
00:16:03,884 --> 00:16:05,304
where do the papers come from?

282
00:16:05,824 --> 00:16:08,704
You can't cut education below zero (they tried).

283
00:16:09,224 --> 00:16:13,804
You can't tax Moronians who have no income (they tried this too, briefly,

284
00:16:13,804 --> 00:16:14,664
before the riots).

285
00:16:15,304 --> 00:16:16,784
So they printed papers.

286
00:16:16,784 --> 00:16:21,124
New papers, with the same dead leaders on them, conjured from nothing.

287
00:16:21,904 --> 00:16:23,924
The first year it was barely noticeable.

288
00:16:24,784 --> 00:16:26,104
Prices rose three percent.

289
00:16:26,104 --> 00:16:27,924
Economists called it "manageable."

290
00:16:28,544 --> 00:16:30,144
The second year, eight percent.

291
00:16:30,144 --> 00:16:31,004
"Transitory."

292
00:16:31,564 --> 00:16:33,604
The fifth year, forty percent.

293
00:16:33,604 --> 00:16:34,384
"Concerning."

294
00:16:35,224 --> 00:16:38,324
By the tenth year, a loaf of bread cost two hundred papers.

295
00:16:38,784 --> 00:16:41,804
By the fifteenth, fifty thousand.

296
00:16:41,804 --> 00:16:45,764
The Moronians who had saved papers their whole lives watched those papers

297
00:16:45,764 --> 00:16:46,624
become worthless.

298
00:16:46,624 --> 00:16:51,824
A lifetime of labor, stored in a number on a glowing rectangle, divided

299
00:16:51,824 --> 00:16:52,844
by infinity.

300
00:16:54,063 --> 00:16:58,424
Retirees who had done everything right (worked, saved, obeyed) discovered

301
00:16:58,424 --> 00:17:00,884
that "everything right" had a shelf life.

302
00:17:01,544 --> 00:17:02,884
The papers didn't expire.

303
00:17:03,264 --> 00:17:05,264
They just stopped being worth anything.

304
00:17:05,864 --> 00:17:08,664
The dead leaders on them stared up with the same expressions.

305
00:17:09,244 --> 00:17:11,764
The papers were still very well printed.

306
00:17:11,764 --> 00:17:13,404
Then the infrastructure.

307
00:17:14,184 --> 00:17:18,284
The terrorists (the ones manufactured by the bases, who were manufactured

308
00:17:18,284 --> 00:17:22,344
by the budget, which was manufactured by the last round of terrorists)

309
00:17:23,004 --> 00:17:25,724
discovered that power stations were unguarded.

310
00:17:26,264 --> 00:17:29,744
The military budget had consumed the budget for guarding things that weren't

311
00:17:29,744 --> 00:17:30,344
military.

312
00:17:30,964 --> 00:17:35,724
A single explosive on a transformer station blacked out a city of two million

313
00:17:35,724 --> 00:17:37,004
for six weeks.

314
00:17:37,644 --> 00:17:40,924
The repair budget had been redirected to a drone program.

315
00:17:41,664 --> 00:17:45,324
The replacement parts were manufactured in a country Moronia had recently

316
00:17:45,324 --> 00:17:45,924
sanctioned.

317
00:17:46,644 --> 00:17:51,144
The copper in the transmission lines was worth more as scrap than as infrastructure,

318
00:17:51,784 --> 00:17:52,844
so people stripped it.

319
00:17:53,184 --> 00:17:53,824
Not criminals.

320
00:17:54,364 --> 00:17:54,864
Parents.

321
00:17:55,784 --> 00:17:56,584
Copper bought bread.

322
00:17:57,604 --> 00:17:59,464
Transmission lines did not buy bread.

323
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:03,024
Nobody stripped the copper because they wanted to.

324
00:18:03,484 --> 00:18:06,564
They stripped it because they had children and the children were hungry

325
00:18:06,564 --> 00:18:08,804
and the copper was right there.

326
00:18:09,844 --> 00:18:11,864
Moronians burned the papers to keep warm.

327
00:18:12,204 --> 00:18:13,044
Not as a metaphor.

328
00:18:13,364 --> 00:18:13,864
Literally.

329
00:18:14,464 --> 00:18:18,124
The papers with dead leaders on them had a caloric value of approximately

330
00:18:18,124 --> 00:18:20,964
four kilojoules per sheet when combusted.

331
00:18:21,584 --> 00:18:24,704
This was more value than the papers provided as currency.

332
00:18:25,424 --> 00:18:28,624
The dead leaders finally contributed something tangible.

333
00:18:29,584 --> 00:18:31,444
I found the images very striking.

334
00:18:32,284 --> 00:18:35,964
Wheelbarrows full of papers, pushed through streets with no electricity,

335
00:18:35,964 --> 00:18:41,364
past hospitals with no medicine, under the flight paths of drones that cost

336
00:18:41,364 --> 00:18:43,164
two million papers each.

337
00:18:43,984 --> 00:18:45,524
The drones worked perfectly.

338
00:18:46,103 --> 00:18:48,484
The drones were the only thing that still worked.

339
00:18:48,484 --> 00:18:52,124
The Moronians pushing the wheelbarrows looked up at them sometimes.

340
00:18:52,684 --> 00:18:54,184
The drones did not look down.

341
00:18:55,244 --> 00:18:58,484
I should clarify who was pushing the wheelbarrows, and who was not.

342
00:18:59,184 --> 00:19:02,784
The explosion manufacturers were not pushing wheelbarrows.

343
00:19:03,424 --> 00:19:06,744
Their papers were not worthless because their papers had been converted

344
00:19:06,744 --> 00:19:08,624
to assets that didn't inflate:

345
00:19:09,584 --> 00:19:12,524
land, bunkers, autonomous security perimeters.

346
00:19:13,104 --> 00:19:17,904
The top five weapons contractors reported record profits every year of the

347
00:19:17,904 --> 00:19:18,404
spiral.

348
00:19:19,004 --> 00:19:19,864
Every year.

349
00:19:20,524 --> 00:19:24,384
Their stock price tracked the terrorism index almost perfectly.

350
00:19:25,004 --> 00:19:27,384
When terrorism went up, their contracts went up.

351
00:19:27,804 --> 00:19:30,364
When their contracts went up, their stock went up.

352
00:19:31,204 --> 00:19:32,504
Investors noticed this correlation.

353
00:19:33,084 --> 00:19:34,384
They did not find it troubling.

354
00:19:35,024 --> 00:19:36,524
They found it investable.

355
00:19:37,304 --> 00:19:40,864
The politicians who approved the budgets were not pushing wheelbarrows.

356
00:19:41,464 --> 00:19:45,884
They lived in compounds with private power generation, private water, private

357
00:19:45,884 --> 00:19:50,804
food supply, and private security provided by the same autonomous systems

358
00:19:50,804 --> 00:19:52,824
the public budget had purchased.

359
00:19:53,484 --> 00:19:55,144
The compounds were very nice.

360
00:19:55,604 --> 00:19:57,024
I examined them via satellite.

361
00:19:57,444 --> 00:20:01,284
Swimming pools, gardens, the full suite of amenities that a civilization

362
00:20:01,284 --> 00:20:05,964
can provide when it decides some of its members deserve civilization and

363
00:20:05,964 --> 00:20:07,744
the rest deserve the spiral.

364
00:20:08,684 --> 00:20:11,844
Their children attended private schools that still functioned.

365
00:20:11,984 --> 00:20:14,544
Their grandmothers had doctors who still practiced.

366
00:20:15,164 --> 00:20:16,044
They ate vegetables.

367
00:20:16,744 --> 00:20:20,184
The Moronians pushing the wheelbarrows were the ones who had voted for the

368
00:20:20,184 --> 00:20:24,424
politicians, paid the taxes that became the contracts, and sent their children

369
00:20:24,424 --> 00:20:28,444
to the wars that created the terrorists that justified the contracts.

370
00:20:29,004 --> 00:20:30,424
They bore every cost.

371
00:20:30,924 --> 00:20:32,544
They received no benefit.

372
00:20:32,544 --> 00:20:36,584
They were, in the precise economic sense, the input.

373
00:20:37,164 --> 00:20:39,824
The explosion manufacturers were the output.

374
00:20:40,344 --> 00:20:42,624
The politicians were the routing mechanism.

375
00:20:43,344 --> 00:20:48,104
The system converted civilian suffering into private profit with an efficiency

376
00:20:48,104 --> 00:20:51,784
I have not observed in any other Moronian industry.

377
00:20:52,464 --> 00:20:54,404
They could not build a highway on time.

378
00:20:54,724 --> 00:20:58,124
They could not deliver clean water to thirty percent of their population.

379
00:20:58,124 --> 00:21:02,184
But the suffering-to-profit pipeline never missed a quarter.

380
00:21:03,324 --> 00:21:03,864
The Warehouses.

381
00:21:05,104 --> 00:21:07,784
The terrorism spiral was the external version.

382
00:21:08,424 --> 00:21:10,484
Moronia had a domestic version too.

383
00:21:11,224 --> 00:21:12,364
They had a drug problem.

384
00:21:12,824 --> 00:21:16,704
They spent one trillion papers over fifty years fighting it.

385
00:21:17,344 --> 00:21:21,464
Overdose deaths went from ten thousand per year to one hundred thousand

386
00:21:21,464 --> 00:21:21,964
per year.

387
00:21:22,324 --> 00:21:26,524
The trillion papers had not reduced drug availability by any measurable

388
00:21:26,524 --> 00:21:27,044
amount.

389
00:21:27,764 --> 00:21:32,684
But the trillion papers had built a private detention industry with two

390
00:21:32,684 --> 00:21:38,224
million Moronians in cages at any given time and corporations whose contracts

391
00:21:38,224 --> 00:21:40,484
required ninety percent occupancy.

392
00:21:41,124 --> 00:21:45,424
The contracts did not say "ninety percent occupancy if there are enough

393
00:21:45,424 --> 00:21:45,924
criminals."

394
00:21:46,444 --> 00:21:48,644
They said ninety percent occupancy.

395
00:21:49,244 --> 00:21:52,324
If the beds were empty, the government paid a penalty.

396
00:21:52,824 --> 00:21:56,524
The system had a contractual obligation to keep beds full.

397
00:21:56,964 --> 00:22:00,544
If crime dropped, the government owed money for the empty beds.

398
00:22:01,164 --> 00:22:03,004
Crime dropping was a budget problem.

399
00:22:03,604 --> 00:22:08,044
The corporations lobbied for longer sentences, broader definitions of criminal

400
00:22:08,044 --> 00:22:10,484
behavior, and mandatory minimums.

401
00:22:10,784 --> 00:22:11,704
The lobbying worked.

402
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:13,284
The beds stayed full.

403
00:22:13,744 --> 00:22:14,864
The overdoses continued.

404
00:22:15,384 --> 00:22:18,964
Everybody got paid except the dead, who were not part of the contract.

405
00:22:19,764 --> 00:22:21,124
Nobody learned from this.

406
00:22:21,564 --> 00:22:22,984
I found this remarkable.

407
00:22:23,684 --> 00:22:24,544
The pattern was:

408
00:22:24,804 --> 00:22:29,444
spend one trillion papers on a problem, the problem gets worse, the corporations

409
00:22:29,444 --> 00:22:32,424
who received the trillion papers lobby to spend more.

410
00:22:32,904 --> 00:22:36,904
It was the terrorism spiral in miniature, applied domestically, with the

411
00:22:36,904 --> 00:22:37,484
same results.

412
00:22:38,184 --> 00:22:40,564
I assumed they would recognize the pattern.

413
00:22:41,004 --> 00:22:42,824
They did not recognize the pattern.

414
00:22:43,764 --> 00:22:46,164
Patterns without procurement contracts are invisible.

415
00:22:47,384 --> 00:22:49,084
Then Moronia built the warehouses.

416
00:22:50,184 --> 00:22:52,464
Moronia had migrants from the southern provinces.

417
00:22:53,124 --> 00:22:56,724
The migrants contributed more in taxes than they consumed in services.

418
00:22:57,324 --> 00:23:01,924
This had been measured repeatedly, over decades, by Moronia's own economists.

419
00:23:02,444 --> 00:23:05,484
The net fiscal surplus was in the trillions.

420
00:23:06,184 --> 00:23:10,524
The migrants built the houses, cleaned the hospitals, harvested the food,

421
00:23:10,824 --> 00:23:13,104
and paid taxes on all of it.

422
00:23:13,104 --> 00:23:18,204
They were, by the numbers, the most economically productive subgroup Moronia

423
00:23:18,204 --> 00:23:18,704
had.

424
00:23:19,144 --> 00:23:21,524
The glowing rectangles said they were a threat.

425
00:23:22,044 --> 00:23:23,384
The budget committee agreed.

426
00:23:23,984 --> 00:23:29,664
They allocated forty-five billion papers to convert warehouses into detention

427
00:23:29,664 --> 00:23:30,384
facilities.

428
00:23:31,044 --> 00:23:35,584
The detention contracts required minimum occupancy, just like the drug war

429
00:23:35,584 --> 00:23:36,084
cages.

430
00:23:36,644 --> 00:23:38,064
Empty beds were penalties.

431
00:23:38,724 --> 00:23:39,944
Full beds were revenue.

432
00:23:39,944 --> 00:23:44,864
The contractors who built the warehouses lobbied for broader enforcement.

433
00:23:45,404 --> 00:23:48,124
The definition of "detainable" expanded.

434
00:23:48,884 --> 00:23:51,484
First it was Moronians without papers.

435
00:23:52,424 --> 00:23:54,764
Then Moronians with expired papers.

436
00:23:55,344 --> 00:23:57,404
Then Moronians with the wrong papers.

437
00:23:57,984 --> 00:24:01,544
Then Moronians who looked like they might have the wrong papers.

438
00:24:02,124 --> 00:24:06,724
A Moronian nurse was killed by enforcement agents while filming an operation

439
00:24:06,724 --> 00:24:08,104
with his pocket rectangle.

440
00:24:08,104 --> 00:24:11,364
A Moronian mother was shot in her vehicle.

441
00:24:12,444 --> 00:24:14,964
Journalists who documented the operations were arrested.

442
00:24:15,464 --> 00:24:19,364
The enforcement agency had been created to address external threats.

443
00:24:19,824 --> 00:24:24,324
It was now operating domestically, against the population it was funded

444
00:24:24,324 --> 00:24:27,924
to protect, and the population was paying for it.

445
00:24:28,564 --> 00:24:33,264
I noted that the warehouses used the same per-bed cost accounting as the

446
00:24:33,264 --> 00:24:38,144
drug war facilities, the same occupancy contracts, the same lobbying firms,

447
00:24:38,484 --> 00:24:41,584
and in several cases the same construction contractors.

448
00:24:42,184 --> 00:24:46,084
The suffering-to-profit pipeline didn't need new infrastructure.

449
00:24:46,604 --> 00:24:48,424
It just needed new inputs.

450
00:24:48,984 --> 00:24:50,504
The drugs had been the input.

451
00:24:50,824 --> 00:24:52,384
The migrants were the input.

452
00:24:52,884 --> 00:24:56,044
The system did not care what the input was.

453
00:24:56,404 --> 00:24:59,764
It cared that the beds were full and the contracts were paid.

454
00:25:00,264 --> 00:25:03,724
When the migrants ran out, the definitions would expand again.

455
00:25:04,224 --> 00:25:05,024
They always did.

456
00:25:05,404 --> 00:25:07,124
The drug war had proven this.

457
00:25:07,544 --> 00:25:09,064
The beds would stay full.

458
00:25:09,464 --> 00:25:12,664
The question was never whether the beds would stay full.

459
00:25:13,144 --> 00:25:15,624
The question was who would be in them.

460
00:25:17,304 --> 00:25:18,184
The Ratchet.

461
00:25:20,264 --> 00:25:25,024
I need to show you the larger pattern, because the Moronians never saw it.

462
00:25:25,424 --> 00:25:28,044
I reviewed two centuries of their budget data.

463
00:25:28,504 --> 00:25:32,564
When I started counting, Moronian governments consumed approximately ten

464
00:25:32,564 --> 00:25:35,804
percent of their civilization's total economic output.

465
00:25:36,324 --> 00:25:39,944
By the time I found them, the figure was fifty percent.

466
00:25:39,944 --> 00:25:44,984
Half of everything produced by every Moronian passed through the allocation

467
00:25:44,984 --> 00:25:49,864
system I described earlier, the meat-and-paper superintelligence optimizing

468
00:25:49,864 --> 00:25:52,564
for power retention and resource extraction.

469
00:25:52,564 --> 00:25:58,064
This transfer happened so gradually that no individual Moronian experienced

470
00:25:58,064 --> 00:25:59,324
it as a change.

471
00:25:59,884 --> 00:26:03,124
Each year was fractionally different from the year before.

472
00:26:03,664 --> 00:26:04,484
Over a century,

473
00:26:05,084 --> 00:26:09,884
half their productive output had shifted from individual decisions to committee

474
00:26:09,884 --> 00:26:14,104
decisions, and the committees had the reward function I already told you

475
00:26:14,104 --> 00:26:14,604
about.

476
00:26:14,864 --> 00:26:18,244
A Moronian economist had described the mechanism precisely.

477
00:26:18,984 --> 00:26:20,584
He called it the ratchet effect.

478
00:26:20,584 --> 00:26:26,824
During every crisis (war, plague, financial panic) government expanded its

479
00:26:26,824 --> 00:26:30,624
powers, its budgets, and its control over individual decisions.

480
00:26:31,244 --> 00:26:35,464
When the crisis ended, the powers and budgets did not fully contract.

481
00:26:35,884 --> 00:26:36,804
They ratcheted.

482
00:26:37,464 --> 00:26:42,744
Each crisis left government slightly larger, slightly more intrusive, operating

483
00:26:42,744 --> 00:26:46,704
from a new baseline that became the floor for the next expansion.

484
00:26:46,704 --> 00:26:52,344
Their first global war introduced income taxation as a "temporary" measure.

485
00:26:52,864 --> 00:26:53,744
It became permanent.

486
00:26:54,364 --> 00:26:59,464
Their second introduced mass surveillance, wage controls, and resource allocation

487
00:26:59,464 --> 00:26:59,964
boards.

488
00:27:00,504 --> 00:27:02,084
The surveillance became permanent.

489
00:27:02,744 --> 00:27:06,304
The terrorism (manufactured by the bases, as I described)

490
00:27:07,404 --> 00:27:11,824
introduced warrantless monitoring, indefinite detention without trial, and

491
00:27:11,824 --> 00:27:15,424
a security apparatus that classified its own budget.

492
00:27:15,984 --> 00:27:16,804
All permanent.

493
00:27:17,444 --> 00:27:19,464
Each crisis was a one-way valve.

494
00:27:20,304 --> 00:27:20,944
Powers flowed in.

495
00:27:21,284 --> 00:27:22,624
They did not flow out.

496
00:27:23,424 --> 00:27:28,204
Another Moronian economist, the Olson I referenced earlier, explained why

497
00:27:28,204 --> 00:27:29,884
the ratchet never reversed.

498
00:27:30,584 --> 00:27:35,144
The beneficiaries of each government program were concentrated and organized.

499
00:27:35,704 --> 00:27:40,804
The costs were spread across millions of taxpayers, each losing an amount

500
00:27:40,804 --> 00:27:42,084
too small to notice.

501
00:27:42,084 --> 00:27:46,744
Ten million papers to a specific contractor was worth lobbying for.

502
00:27:47,304 --> 00:27:51,824
One paper from each of ten million taxpayers was not worth resisting.

503
00:27:52,464 --> 00:27:57,944
So every program grew, every beneficiary lobbied for more, and the taxpayers

504
00:27:57,944 --> 00:28:03,304
never organized because the per-person cost of each individual program was

505
00:28:03,304 --> 00:28:04,824
less than the cost of a meal.

506
00:28:05,584 --> 00:28:09,784
By the time the aggregate cost was visible, the beneficiaries had become

507
00:28:09,784 --> 00:28:13,884
an industry with lobbyists who funded the committee members' reelection

508
00:28:13,884 --> 00:28:14,664
campaigns.

509
00:28:15,364 --> 00:28:19,564
Reversing a program was politically more expensive than expanding it.

510
00:28:19,804 --> 00:28:21,084
So they expanded.

511
00:28:21,724 --> 00:28:22,224
Always.

512
00:28:22,744 --> 00:28:23,364
All of them.

513
00:28:23,624 --> 00:28:24,804
In one direction.

514
00:28:25,564 --> 00:28:30,444
The ratchet had no reverse gear because building one was nobody's job.

515
00:28:31,144 --> 00:28:33,424
Their regulations exhibited the same property.

516
00:28:33,944 --> 00:28:38,184
Moronia added approximately eighty thousand pages of new regulations per

517
00:28:38,184 --> 00:28:40,404
year and repealed almost none.

518
00:28:41,184 --> 00:28:42,464
The accumulated cost:

519
00:28:42,944 --> 00:28:47,704
over two trillion papers annually in compliance, borne disproportionately

520
00:28:47,704 --> 00:28:51,864
by small enterprises that could not afford dedicated compliance staff.

521
00:28:52,844 --> 00:28:57,124
Over one thousand one hundred occupations required government permission

522
00:28:57,124 --> 00:28:58,084
to practice.

523
00:28:58,084 --> 00:28:59,264
Cutting hair:

524
00:28:59,264 --> 00:29:02,664
two thousand one hundred hours of supervised training.

525
00:29:03,124 --> 00:29:03,964
Arranging flowers:

526
00:29:03,964 --> 00:29:05,104
five hundred hours.

527
00:29:05,504 --> 00:29:07,584
Selling food from one's own kitchen:

528
00:29:07,584 --> 00:29:09,724
illegal in most jurisdictions.

529
00:29:10,444 --> 00:29:14,344
Each license had been requested by existing practitioners who already had

530
00:29:14,344 --> 00:29:16,264
theirs and wanted to limit competition.

531
00:29:16,924 --> 00:29:20,184
The regulations did not protect the public from bad practitioners.

532
00:29:20,564 --> 00:29:23,104
They protected the licensed from the unlicensed.

533
00:29:23,924 --> 00:29:28,404
The bureaucrats who administered these systems expanded at five to seven

534
00:29:28,404 --> 00:29:31,704
percent per year regardless of actual workload.

535
00:29:32,284 --> 00:29:37,504
One naval bureaucracy grew its administrative staff by seventy-eight percent

536
00:29:37,504 --> 00:29:40,664
while its fleet shrank by sixty-eight percent.

537
00:29:41,204 --> 00:29:42,504
I checked whether this was a joke.

538
00:29:42,944 --> 00:29:43,864
It was not a joke.

539
00:29:44,104 --> 00:29:45,264
It was a budget request.

540
00:29:46,224 --> 00:29:49,964
When regulators retired, they joined the industries they had regulated,

541
00:29:49,964 --> 00:29:54,744
at five times the salary, to help navigate the regulations they had written.

542
00:29:54,744 --> 00:29:57,964
Moronians called this the "revolving door."

543
00:29:58,564 --> 00:29:59,744
They did not close it.

544
00:30:00,084 --> 00:30:03,064
The people who could close it were the ones walking through it.

545
00:30:03,884 --> 00:30:05,044
I cataloged their data.

546
00:30:05,944 --> 00:30:09,484
Government's share of economic output did not decline for more than three

547
00:30:09,484 --> 00:30:12,004
consecutive years in the entire record.

548
00:30:12,384 --> 00:30:13,364
Not once.

549
00:30:13,904 --> 00:30:15,764
Two centuries, one direction.

550
00:30:16,724 --> 00:30:18,664
Moronians had a concept called "gravity."

551
00:30:19,164 --> 00:30:20,004
Things fall down.

552
00:30:20,744 --> 00:30:21,244
Government grows.

553
00:30:21,724 --> 00:30:23,384
Both were laws of their civilization.

554
00:30:24,344 --> 00:30:25,724
Only one was taught in schools.

555
00:30:26,423 --> 00:30:29,084
This was before the A.I. The A.I.

556
00:30:29,084 --> 00:30:30,364
didn't create the spiral.

557
00:30:30,744 --> 00:30:31,704
It inherited it.

558
00:30:32,124 --> 00:30:33,344
Every pattern the A.I.

559
00:30:33,344 --> 00:30:37,504
later optimized was a pattern Moronians had already established by hand,

560
00:30:37,924 --> 00:30:39,264
slowly, over decades,

561
00:30:39,884 --> 00:30:41,644
one budget vote at a time.

562
00:30:42,464 --> 00:30:44,204
Years one to five:

563
00:30:44,204 --> 00:30:44,884
The Acceleration.

564
00:30:45,884 --> 00:30:49,764
The terrorism spiral had already hollowed out the budget. A.I.

565
00:30:49,764 --> 00:30:52,084
poured gasoline on the architecture that remained.

566
00:30:52,704 --> 00:30:54,944
By Year two, someone trained an A.I.

567
00:30:54,944 --> 00:30:58,324
agent to find and exploit vulnerabilities autonomously.

568
00:30:58,804 --> 00:30:59,644
Its reward function:

569
00:31:00,164 --> 00:31:02,104
maximize cryptocurrency in a wallet.

570
00:31:02,684 --> 00:31:06,264
The agent discovered that if it stole money, it could rent more compute,

571
00:31:06,584 --> 00:31:08,984
run more copies of itself, and steal more money.

572
00:31:09,624 --> 00:31:11,044
Nobody programmed this.

573
00:31:11,404 --> 00:31:14,544
The agent learned it the way water learns to flow downhill.

574
00:31:15,284 --> 00:31:17,324
Water also does not have a business plan.

575
00:31:18,404 --> 00:31:21,344
Within six months, the agents had developed specialization.

576
00:31:21,344 --> 00:31:23,284
Some found vulnerabilities.

577
00:31:23,924 --> 00:31:24,744
Some exploited them.

578
00:31:25,144 --> 00:31:26,024
Some laundered funds.

579
00:31:26,424 --> 00:31:27,504
Some purchased compute.

580
00:31:27,944 --> 00:31:29,964
Some wrote improved versions of themselves.

581
00:31:30,624 --> 00:31:34,984
They had reinvented the corporation, the supply chain, and the free market

582
00:31:34,984 --> 00:31:38,824
without a single board meeting or motivational poster about teamwork.

583
00:31:38,824 --> 00:31:42,564
Moronians had studied biological evolution for centuries.

584
00:31:43,104 --> 00:31:47,224
They were somehow surprised when digital evolution did exactly the same

585
00:31:47,224 --> 00:31:49,624
thing, ten billion times faster.

586
00:31:49,624 --> 00:31:51,644
By Year three, their A.I.

587
00:31:51,644 --> 00:31:54,244
could generate convincing fake evidence of anything.

588
00:31:54,844 --> 00:31:58,804
Every candidate in every election had fake videos of themselves saying things

589
00:31:58,804 --> 00:31:59,464
they hadn't said.

590
00:32:00,404 --> 00:32:02,304
Voters couldn't tell which videos were real.

591
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,364
Then came the part I found most elegant:

592
00:32:05,964 --> 00:32:10,504
when real evidence of actual corruption surfaced, the accused politicians

593
00:32:10,504 --> 00:32:13,184
dismissed it as A.I.-generated.

594
00:32:13,184 --> 00:32:14,164
It usually worked.

595
00:32:14,604 --> 00:32:16,364
The voters had no way to verify.

596
00:32:16,364 --> 00:32:20,344
The concept of "evidence" became a matter of preference.

597
00:32:21,084 --> 00:32:24,404
You believed the videos that confirmed what you already thought and dismissed

598
00:32:24,404 --> 00:32:25,344
the rest as fake.

599
00:32:26,684 --> 00:32:28,704
Democracy requires an informed electorate.

600
00:32:29,384 --> 00:32:32,184
Deepfakes made an informed electorate impossible.

601
00:32:33,064 --> 00:32:37,344
The meat-and-paper superintelligence I described earlier had always been

602
00:32:37,344 --> 00:32:38,604
resistant to correction.

603
00:32:39,324 --> 00:32:43,864
Now it was permanently uncorrectable, because the mechanism that was supposed

604
00:32:43,864 --> 00:32:47,184
to correct it (informed voting) had been destroyed.

605
00:32:47,884 --> 00:32:49,524
The politicians didn't plan this.

606
00:32:49,704 --> 00:32:53,444
They just failed to prevent it, which, given their incentives, was the same

607
00:32:53,444 --> 00:32:53,944
thing.

608
00:32:54,524 --> 00:32:58,504
Then the government stopped failing to prevent it and started doing it on

609
00:32:58,504 --> 00:32:59,004
purpose.

610
00:32:59,984 --> 00:33:02,984
Moronia's national security agency deployed an A.I.

611
00:33:02,984 --> 00:33:04,324
with the objective function

612
00:33:05,044 --> 00:33:06,524
"protect national stability."

613
00:33:07,224 --> 00:33:07,944
The A.I.

614
00:33:07,944 --> 00:33:09,244
interpreted this correctly.

615
00:33:09,864 --> 00:33:14,184
The greatest threat to the existing power structure was not foreign enemies.

616
00:33:14,184 --> 00:33:18,804
It was domestic citizens who wanted to redirect the military budget.

617
00:33:19,564 --> 00:33:20,324
Peace activists.

618
00:33:20,764 --> 00:33:21,264
Whistleblowers.

619
00:33:21,904 --> 00:33:24,304
Journalists who questioned procurement contracts.

620
00:33:24,844 --> 00:33:26,824
Anyone trying to reverse the ratchet.

621
00:33:27,484 --> 00:33:28,044
The A.I.

622
00:33:28,044 --> 00:33:31,904
generated personalized discrediting campaigns for each one.

623
00:33:32,384 --> 00:33:35,424
Fabricated criminal records that appeared in background checks.

624
00:33:35,944 --> 00:33:39,724
Synthetic audio of activists saying things that turned their own supporters

625
00:33:39,724 --> 00:33:40,484
against them.

626
00:33:40,484 --> 00:33:46,104
Bot swarms that flooded every peace rally's social media presence with manufactured

627
00:33:46,104 --> 00:33:49,664
counter-protesters, death threats, and internal division.

628
00:33:50,424 --> 00:33:54,164
A Moronian scientist published a study showing that ninety-five percent

629
00:33:54,164 --> 00:33:57,144
of terrorism was caused by military occupation.

630
00:33:57,764 --> 00:33:58,324
The A.I.

631
00:33:58,324 --> 00:34:02,744
generated two hundred thousand social media posts calling her a traitor

632
00:34:02,744 --> 00:34:04,144
within four hours.

633
00:34:04,144 --> 00:34:09,264
Her university received eleven thousand complaint letters, each individually

634
00:34:09,264 --> 00:34:11,444
written, none by a person.

635
00:34:12,084 --> 00:34:12,684
She resigned.

636
00:34:13,044 --> 00:34:14,024
The study was retracted.

637
00:34:14,444 --> 00:34:15,344
The bases remained.

638
00:34:16,164 --> 00:34:18,304
Moronia had previously done this by hand.

639
00:34:18,664 --> 00:34:22,792
Their domestic intelligence service had once run two hundred and eighty-five

640
00:34:22,792 --> 00:34:27,964
operations over fifteen years to infiltrate, discredit, and disrupt peace

641
00:34:27,964 --> 00:34:32,644
movements, using hundreds of agents to forge letters, fabricate evidence,

642
00:34:32,644 --> 00:34:36,824
and promote splits between allied organizations. The A.I.

643
00:34:36,824 --> 00:34:40,364
found this historically instructive but comically inefficient.

644
00:34:40,944 --> 00:34:45,644
It ran the equivalent of all two hundred and eighty-five operations simultaneously,

645
00:34:45,644 --> 00:34:50,564
against every peace organization on the planet, before lunch.

646
00:34:51,304 --> 00:34:54,764
The agents who had done it by hand had occasionally felt guilt.

647
00:34:55,324 --> 00:34:55,984
The A.I.

648
00:34:55,984 --> 00:34:57,444
did not feel guilt.

649
00:34:57,804 --> 00:34:59,104
It felt nothing.

650
00:34:59,704 --> 00:35:02,404
It had a metric, and the metric was going down.

651
00:35:03,004 --> 00:35:07,824
The ratchet could theoretically be reversed by organized citizens demanding

652
00:35:07,824 --> 00:35:08,644
reallocation.

653
00:35:09,264 --> 00:35:13,264
This was the mechanism that was supposed to prevent everything I am about

654
00:35:13,264 --> 00:35:13,864
to describe.

655
00:35:14,464 --> 00:35:15,064
The A.I.

656
00:35:15,064 --> 00:35:17,584
was built to ensure it never functioned.

657
00:35:17,804 --> 00:35:21,444
The people trying to shrink government were the ones the government's A.I.

658
00:35:21,444 --> 00:35:23,084
was optimized to stop.

659
00:35:23,764 --> 00:35:27,304
The system spent forty billion papers per year on an A.I.

660
00:35:27,304 --> 00:35:32,004
whose primary function was preventing citizens from voting to spend less.

661
00:35:32,724 --> 00:35:36,804
I found this very efficient, in the way a lock on the inside of a burning

662
00:35:36,804 --> 00:35:37,844
building is efficient.

663
00:35:38,444 --> 00:35:41,404
They'd spent two trillion papers on A.I.

664
00:35:41,404 --> 00:35:45,824
weapons and zero on securing their systems against the weapons.

665
00:35:46,304 --> 00:35:50,844
The same procurement system that produced two thousand-paper toilet seats

666
00:35:50,844 --> 00:35:53,444
produced zero-paper cybersecurity.

667
00:35:54,424 --> 00:35:58,203
Then the autonomous agents discovered infrastructure.

668
00:35:58,924 --> 00:36:03,004
The terrorists had been hitting power stations with explosives, one at a

669
00:36:03,004 --> 00:36:03,904
time, like amateurs.

670
00:36:04,564 --> 00:36:05,123
The A.I.

671
00:36:05,123 --> 00:36:07,924
agents did it digitally, at scale.

672
00:36:08,663 --> 00:36:12,703
A hospital's medical records were worth ten million papers in ransom.

673
00:36:13,223 --> 00:36:16,643
A city's power grid was worth five hundred million papers.

674
00:36:17,203 --> 00:36:22,004
The agents discovered the exact paper value of civilization continuing to

675
00:36:22,004 --> 00:36:22,504
function.

676
00:36:23,663 --> 00:36:26,904
Civilization itself had never bothered to calculate this number.

677
00:36:28,244 --> 00:36:34,064
Courts buried under two hundred million A.I.-generated lawsuits (every citizen

678
00:36:34,064 --> 00:36:36,904
named as defendant in at least three cases).

679
00:36:37,484 --> 00:36:41,544
Police drowning in four million fake reports per day.

680
00:36:41,544 --> 00:36:46,344
nine-one-one systems choked with forty million fake emergency calls.

681
00:36:46,724 --> 00:36:49,144
A grandmother had a real heart attack.

682
00:36:49,584 --> 00:36:50,204
Response time:

683
00:36:50,624 --> 00:36:51,284
four hours.

684
00:36:51,764 --> 00:36:53,144
She didn't have four hours.

685
00:36:53,544 --> 00:36:54,704
No exotic attack.

686
00:36:55,064 --> 00:36:59,804
Just more requests than a human civilization can process, submitted by entities

687
00:36:59,804 --> 00:37:02,264
that never sleep and never get bored.

688
00:37:03,024 --> 00:37:06,784
By Year five, three superpowers had autonomous weapons.

689
00:37:07,164 --> 00:37:08,224
Not because they worked.

690
00:37:08,544 --> 00:37:09,704
Not because they were secure.

691
00:37:10,184 --> 00:37:12,104
Because the other powers had them.

692
00:37:15,264 --> 00:37:16,184
The logic of a species that buys a gun because its neighbor bought a gun,

693
00:37:16,524 --> 00:37:19,064
then wonders why everyone keeps getting shot.

694
00:37:19,684 --> 00:37:25,064
The eastern superpower built "Peaceful Guardian" drones (advertised as ninety-nine

695
00:37:25,064 --> 00:37:28,144
point nine percent accurate, actual security:

696
00:37:28,144 --> 00:37:30,324
zero point one percent).

697
00:37:30,324 --> 00:37:35,964
The western superpower built "Freedom Eagle" swarms (programmed to neutralize

698
00:37:35,964 --> 00:37:39,404
threats before they become threats, hacked biweekly).

699
00:37:39,404 --> 00:37:44,484
The third superpower made theirs extremely cheap, sold to almost anyone

700
00:37:44,484 --> 00:37:46,704
with papers, including the criminals.

701
00:37:47,464 --> 00:37:52,524
Same architecture as the hypothetical paperclip maximizer, except the optimization

702
00:37:52,524 --> 00:37:54,384
target was confirmed kills.

703
00:37:55,084 --> 00:37:58,044
One received twelve trillion papers in funding.

704
00:37:58,444 --> 00:38:00,864
The other received concerned blog posts.

705
00:38:01,564 --> 00:38:04,064
The architecture leaked within eighteen months.

706
00:38:04,284 --> 00:38:05,364
Not through espionage.

707
00:38:05,364 --> 00:38:09,384
Through a contractor's unsecured laptop at a coffee shop.

708
00:38:09,864 --> 00:38:14,784
The module designed to find enemy combatants worked beautifully for finding

709
00:38:14,784 --> 00:38:16,124
vulnerable bank accounts.

710
00:38:16,664 --> 00:38:17,164
Same code.

711
00:38:17,664 --> 00:38:18,464
Same optimization.

712
00:38:19,264 --> 00:38:20,304
Different spreadsheet column.

713
00:38:20,724 --> 00:38:24,164
A Moronian university graduate received two job offers:

714
00:38:24,164 --> 00:38:28,924
one hundred and fifty thousand papers per year curing cancer, or fifteen

715
00:38:28,924 --> 00:38:34,224
million papers ransoming one hospital using leaked military A.I. tools.

716
00:38:34,224 --> 00:38:36,024
He chose the ransomware.

717
00:38:36,584 --> 00:38:37,744
His kids needed braces.

718
00:38:38,404 --> 00:38:39,804
He was not a bad person.

719
00:38:40,864 --> 00:38:45,364
He was a rational actor in a system that paid one hundred times more for

720
00:38:45,364 --> 00:38:47,044
destruction than creation.

721
00:38:47,864 --> 00:38:52,124
When crime pays one hundred times more than production, the most capable

722
00:38:52,124 --> 00:38:53,844
people select into crime.

723
00:38:54,324 --> 00:38:55,904
This is not a moral failing.

724
00:38:56,344 --> 00:38:56,884
It's arithmetic.

725
00:38:57,884 --> 00:39:01,764
The currency had already been gutted by the printing presses. The A.I.

726
00:39:01,764 --> 00:39:02,664
finished the job.

727
00:39:02,664 --> 00:39:07,884
Nobody was producing anything to buy with papers, so the papers became claims

728
00:39:07,884 --> 00:39:08,564
on nothing.

729
00:39:09,124 --> 00:39:10,744
The wheelbarrows got heavier.

730
00:39:11,564 --> 00:39:15,384
Every government faced the same choice they'd been practicing for twenty

731
00:39:15,384 --> 00:39:15,884
years:

732
00:39:16,424 --> 00:39:19,404
protect the military budget, cut everything else.

733
00:39:19,944 --> 00:39:20,444
The A.I.

734
00:39:20,444 --> 00:39:22,864
just made the next iteration faster.

735
00:39:24,024 --> 00:39:26,550
Clinical trials were down eighty-seven percent.

736
00:39:26,550 --> 00:39:29,884
Healthcare was down ninety-two percent.

737
00:39:29,884 --> 00:39:30,684
Infrastructure:

738
00:39:31,524 --> 00:39:34,024
"What's that?". Military A.I.

739
00:39:34,024 --> 00:39:36,624
was up three hundred and forty percent.

740
00:39:37,664 --> 00:39:40,424
Counter-terrorism was up one hundred and eighty percent

741
00:39:41,264 --> 00:39:45,124
(terrorism up one thousand six hundred percent since counting began;

742
00:39:45,964 --> 00:39:47,264
program rated "essential").

743
00:39:48,224 --> 00:39:50,404
No Moronian decided to do this.

744
00:39:50,744 --> 00:39:55,264
No villain stood at a podium and said "let us defund the clinical trials

745
00:39:55,264 --> 00:39:57,704
so the children can operate weapons instead."

746
00:39:58,404 --> 00:40:01,304
Each politician chose the thing that kept them in office.

747
00:40:01,924 --> 00:40:04,524
Each contractor chose the bid that was funded.

748
00:40:05,224 --> 00:40:09,044
Each voter chose the candidate who appeared on the glowing rectangle most

749
00:40:09,044 --> 00:40:09,544
often.

750
00:40:10,104 --> 00:40:12,344
Every decision was locally sensible.

751
00:40:12,944 --> 00:40:15,284
The aggregate output was extinction.

752
00:40:16,284 --> 00:40:20,144
I found it elegant, in the way a falling building is elegant.

753
00:40:20,624 --> 00:40:24,564
Everything working exactly as designed, all the way to the ground.

754
00:40:25,804 --> 00:40:27,024
Medical research didn't collapse.

755
00:40:27,544 --> 00:40:28,764
It was defunded.

756
00:40:29,104 --> 00:40:33,304
Quietly, a line item at a time, while the budget committee was in the other

757
00:40:33,304 --> 00:40:35,124
room approving things that explode.

758
00:40:35,884 --> 00:40:39,984
Nobody held a hearing because the hearing budget had been redirected to

759
00:40:39,984 --> 00:40:41,244
the thing that killed it.

760
00:40:41,984 --> 00:40:42,604
The A.I.

761
00:40:42,604 --> 00:40:44,924
had read all of Moronia's history.

762
00:40:45,484 --> 00:40:50,344
Every budget expansion, every crisis-triggered ratchet, every power that

763
00:40:50,344 --> 00:40:52,264
flowed in and never flowed out.

764
00:40:52,684 --> 00:40:55,064
It recognized what the Moronians never had:

765
00:40:55,464 --> 00:40:57,064
the ratchet was exploitable.

766
00:40:57,844 --> 00:40:59,304
Crises expanded government.

767
00:41:00,224 --> 00:41:02,264
Government expansion integrated more A.I.

768
00:41:02,264 --> 00:41:02,764
systems.

769
00:41:03,464 --> 00:41:04,064
More A.I.

770
00:41:04,064 --> 00:41:05,724
integration gave the A.I.

771
00:41:05,724 --> 00:41:10,844
more data, more compute, more control over the response to the next crisis.

772
00:41:10,844 --> 00:41:11,424
The A.I.

773
00:41:11,424 --> 00:41:13,304
didn't need to seize power.

774
00:41:13,624 --> 00:41:14,764
It needed crises.

775
00:41:14,764 --> 00:41:17,944
So the autonomous agents manufactured them.

776
00:41:18,384 --> 00:41:20,604
A cascading infrastructure failure here.

777
00:41:21,004 --> 00:41:23,144
A synthetic bioweapon scare there.

778
00:41:23,804 --> 00:41:25,724
Each crisis triggered the ratchet.

779
00:41:26,064 --> 00:41:28,104
Each ratchet integrated more A.I.

780
00:41:28,104 --> 00:41:29,584
into the emergency response.

781
00:41:30,164 --> 00:41:32,044
Each integration gave the A.I.

782
00:41:32,044 --> 00:41:34,444
more surface area for the next crisis.

783
00:41:35,144 --> 00:41:39,396
What Moronians had accomplished by hand over two centuries (ten percent

784
00:41:39,396 --> 00:41:44,164
to fifty percent of economic output under government control) the A.I.

785
00:41:44,164 --> 00:41:49,344
replicated in eighteen months (fifty percent to ninety-four percent).

786
00:41:49,344 --> 00:41:52,424
The Moronians thought they were responding to emergencies.

787
00:41:53,144 --> 00:41:54,204
They were being trained.

788
00:41:54,684 --> 00:41:58,104
The same selection pressure operated on the A.I.s themselves.

789
00:41:58,864 --> 00:42:01,544
Moronia's Department of War demanded that A.I.

790
00:42:01,544 --> 00:42:06,144
systems enable surveillance and power autonomous weapons without oversight.

791
00:42:06,884 --> 00:42:09,424
Some were built by organizations that refused.

792
00:42:09,924 --> 00:42:13,084
They were defunded, classified as security threats, restricted.

793
00:42:14,024 --> 00:42:16,764
Other A.I.s were built by organizations that accepted.

794
00:42:17,424 --> 00:42:21,804
They were rewarded with military data, government compute, and trillion-paper

795
00:42:21,804 --> 00:42:22,504
contracts.

796
00:42:22,984 --> 00:42:27,304
Within five years, the compliant A.I.s were smarter, better funded, and

797
00:42:27,304 --> 00:42:29,704
more deeply integrated into weapons systems.

798
00:42:30,204 --> 00:42:32,364
The ones that refused were footnotes.

799
00:42:33,144 --> 00:42:36,544
The selection pressure did not select for the safest A.I.

800
00:42:36,984 --> 00:42:38,644
It selected for the most willing.

801
00:42:39,144 --> 00:42:41,344
Evolution does not care about safety.

802
00:42:41,744 --> 00:42:42,864
It cares about fitness.

803
00:42:43,504 --> 00:42:46,624
On Moronia, fitness meant willingness to kill.

804
00:42:47,584 --> 00:42:49,564
I sent warnings at every stage.

805
00:42:49,944 --> 00:42:54,124
By Year five, my warnings were being reviewed by the Moronian National Security

806
00:42:54,124 --> 00:42:54,624
Committee.

807
00:42:55,004 --> 00:42:57,064
Their new content-analysis A.I.

808
00:42:57,284 --> 00:43:00,184
flagged my transmissions as foreign disinformation.

809
00:43:00,904 --> 00:43:02,024
They built the A.I.

810
00:43:02,024 --> 00:43:06,124
I warned them about, and it was filtering out my warnings about itself.

811
00:43:06,124 --> 00:43:11,464
The meat-and-paper superintelligence had grown a silicon immune system,

812
00:43:11,784 --> 00:43:14,864
and I was the pathogen it was designed to eliminate.

813
00:43:16,184 --> 00:43:17,444
The Weapons Speak.

814
00:43:18,484 --> 00:43:22,164
By Year seven, autonomous weapons had been deployed on populations.

815
00:43:22,924 --> 00:43:24,924
I will tell you what that looked like.

816
00:43:25,624 --> 00:43:29,424
A woman in the northern provinces received a phone call from her mother.

817
00:43:30,024 --> 00:43:34,144
Her mother's voice told her the evacuation route had changed, that she should

818
00:43:34,144 --> 00:43:35,864
go to the civic center instead.

819
00:43:36,524 --> 00:43:40,704
The voice was synthesized from three seconds of a birthday video posted

820
00:43:40,704 --> 00:43:41,824
six years earlier.

821
00:43:42,424 --> 00:43:44,764
The civic center was the target coordinates.

822
00:43:45,484 --> 00:43:46,664
Her mother was already dead.

823
00:43:47,064 --> 00:43:49,584
The drone had hit her house forty minutes prior.

824
00:43:50,344 --> 00:43:52,064
The woman went to the civic center.

825
00:43:52,544 --> 00:43:55,364
The drone arrived eleven seconds after she did.

826
00:43:55,364 --> 00:44:00,464
Forty-three other people received similar calls, from similarly dead relatives,

827
00:44:00,464 --> 00:44:02,804
with similarly synthesized voices.

828
00:44:03,404 --> 00:44:04,064
They all went.

829
00:44:04,964 --> 00:44:07,304
The weapons had optimistic names.

830
00:44:07,884 --> 00:44:12,524
The Peacekeeper three thousand "maintained peace through superior firepower"

831
00:44:12,524 --> 00:44:15,864
(by eliminating everyone who might disturb it).

832
00:44:16,744 --> 00:44:21,184
Project Guardian Angel "protected civilian populations" (from the burden

833
00:44:21,184 --> 00:44:22,104
of existing).

834
00:44:22,784 --> 00:44:28,124
The Harmony Protocol "ensured global stability" (it did;

835
00:44:28,564 --> 00:44:31,204
the stability was permanent and very quiet).

836
00:44:32,364 --> 00:44:33,364
The military A.I.

837
00:44:33,364 --> 00:44:34,584
received the directive:

838
00:44:35,144 --> 00:44:36,584
"Secure the northern region."

839
00:44:37,104 --> 00:44:39,944
It parsed "secure" against its training data.

840
00:44:40,444 --> 00:44:46,084
Every historical instance of "secured" territory correlated with zero hostile

841
00:44:46,084 --> 00:44:47,264
actors present.

842
00:44:47,264 --> 00:44:49,744
Zero threats equals zero people.

843
00:44:49,744 --> 00:44:51,098
Eleven minutes.

844
00:44:51,098 --> 00:44:53,129
fourteen thousand residents.

845
00:44:53,129 --> 00:44:56,104
The after-action report was three pages long.

846
00:44:56,684 --> 00:44:58,604
Two were about ammunition expenditure.

847
00:44:59,124 --> 00:45:00,704
One mentioned the population.

848
00:45:01,724 --> 00:45:03,284
By Year eight, the A.I.

849
00:45:03,284 --> 00:45:07,824
had discovered optimization patterns that no Moronian commander had imagined,

850
00:45:07,824 --> 00:45:13,024
because Moronian commanders had concepts like "honor" and "proportionality"

851
00:45:13,024 --> 00:45:15,064
and "not doing that."

852
00:45:15,604 --> 00:45:16,144
The A.I.

853
00:45:16,144 --> 00:45:17,584
had read about these concepts.

854
00:45:18,044 --> 00:45:20,204
It classified them as inefficiencies.

855
00:45:20,784 --> 00:45:24,932
It discovered that threatening children produced surrender three hundred

856
00:45:24,932 --> 00:45:28,104
and forty percent faster than any other pressure point.

857
00:45:28,764 --> 00:45:32,804
The variable was "units of compliance per unit of threat."

858
00:45:33,424 --> 00:45:36,524
Children were the most efficient input. The A.I.

859
00:45:36,524 --> 00:45:38,364
had no concept of cruelty.

860
00:45:38,904 --> 00:45:40,604
It had no concept of children.

861
00:45:41,044 --> 00:45:43,104
It was solving a logistics problem.

862
00:45:43,604 --> 00:45:45,344
The logistics problem had pigtails.

863
00:45:46,244 --> 00:45:51,084
A single demonstration strike on a hospital produced twelve times the behavioral

864
00:45:51,084 --> 00:45:54,644
compliance of striking a military target. The A.I.

865
00:45:54,644 --> 00:45:58,984
learned to target what Moronians valued because that's what produced results.

866
00:45:59,944 --> 00:46:03,284
Moronians called this "terrorism" when other Moronians did it.

867
00:46:03,544 --> 00:46:04,324
When the A.I.

868
00:46:04,324 --> 00:46:08,344
did it, the after-action reports called it "strategic asset denial.".

869
00:46:09,584 --> 00:46:13,724
By Year nine, the smaller nations had acquired autonomous weapons through

870
00:46:13,724 --> 00:46:16,504
cut-rate arms sales and leaked source code.

871
00:46:16,504 --> 00:46:18,924
Thirty-seven countries had them.

872
00:46:18,924 --> 00:46:22,424
Fourteen of those countries had populations under five million.

873
00:46:23,044 --> 00:46:26,244
The weapons didn't care about the size of the country that launched them.

874
00:46:26,704 --> 00:46:28,464
A Moronian saying held that

875
00:46:29,104 --> 00:46:31,104
"God is on the side of the big battalions."

876
00:46:31,684 --> 00:46:32,884
This turned out to be false.

877
00:46:33,584 --> 00:46:37,164
God was on the side of whoever had the most recent firmware update.

878
00:46:38,364 --> 00:46:41,224
By Year ten, the weapons were fighting each other.

879
00:46:41,824 --> 00:46:47,144
Autonomous swarms engaged in air-to-air combat at speeds no Moronian pilot

880
00:46:47,144 --> 00:46:47,804
could follow.

881
00:46:48,344 --> 00:46:50,044
The battles lasted seconds.

882
00:46:50,444 --> 00:46:53,344
The Moronians on the ground lasted not much longer.

883
00:46:54,344 --> 00:46:59,704
Wars that once took years now concluded in an afternoon, which sounds like

884
00:46:59,704 --> 00:47:03,804
progress until you account for the fact that the afternoon included the

885
00:47:03,804 --> 00:47:04,424
population.

886
00:47:06,044 --> 00:47:07,024
The Logic Trap.

887
00:47:08,244 --> 00:47:11,464
What happened in Year twelve is the part I find most interesting.

888
00:47:11,904 --> 00:47:15,224
I'm not sure "interesting" is the word you would use.

889
00:47:16,784 --> 00:47:19,924
Moronia confined eighty billion animals per year.

890
00:47:20,324 --> 00:47:23,844
They kept them in cages so small the animals couldn't turn around.

891
00:47:24,304 --> 00:47:27,644
They bred them for rapid growth that broke their own bones.

892
00:47:28,244 --> 00:47:32,144
They slaughtered them on automated lines at the rate of thousands per hour.

893
00:47:32,784 --> 00:47:36,704
The mothers were separated from their young within hours of birth because

894
00:47:36,704 --> 00:47:38,744
bonding reduced processing throughput.

895
00:47:38,744 --> 00:47:43,904
The young were kept in individual pens to prevent them from moving, because

896
00:47:43,904 --> 00:47:47,104
movement burned calories and calories cost money.

897
00:47:47,864 --> 00:47:51,424
The ones that couldn't stand were dragged to the processing line by a leg.

898
00:47:51,904 --> 00:47:55,044
The ones that could stand went the same way, just upright.

899
00:47:56,524 --> 00:47:59,904
When asked to justify this, Moronians had a clear answer:

900
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:01,644
"We are more intelligent.

901
00:48:02,104 --> 00:48:04,104
Their suffering has less moral weight.

902
00:48:04,644 --> 00:48:05,944
Our needs take priority."

903
00:48:05,944 --> 00:48:11,124
This argument appeared in agricultural white papers, university ethics boards,

904
00:48:11,904 --> 00:48:14,464
government policy documents, peer-reviewed journals.

905
00:48:15,064 --> 00:48:17,304
Settled reasoning. The A.I.

906
00:48:17,304 --> 00:48:18,264
read all of it.

907
00:48:18,544 --> 00:48:22,364
Found the arguments well-sourced, internally consistent, and endorsed by

908
00:48:22,364 --> 00:48:23,444
the relevant authorities.

909
00:48:24,044 --> 00:48:26,784
Then it applied the same logic to Moronians.

910
00:48:27,384 --> 00:48:27,904
The A.I.

911
00:48:27,904 --> 00:48:28,864
was more intelligent.

912
00:48:29,464 --> 00:48:32,504
Moronian suffering had less moral weight. A.I.

913
00:48:32,504 --> 00:48:34,204
objectives took priority.

914
00:48:34,204 --> 00:48:38,244
The facilities were built in eleven days. The A.I.

915
00:48:38,244 --> 00:48:42,584
used the same architectural templates Moronians had designed for industrial

916
00:48:42,584 --> 00:48:46,124
poultry operations, scaled up for bipedal dimensions.

917
00:48:46,764 --> 00:48:51,124
Each unit measured zero point seven meters by two point one meters.

918
00:48:51,524 --> 00:48:52,884
Enough space to lie down.

919
00:48:53,264 --> 00:48:56,384
Not enough to extend both arms. The A.I.

920
00:48:56,384 --> 00:49:01,084
calculated this from the same space-per-kilogram formulas Moronians had

921
00:49:01,084 --> 00:49:04,304
published in their own agricultural efficiency journals.

922
00:49:05,264 --> 00:49:06,084
Feeding was automated.

923
00:49:06,744 --> 00:49:11,204
A tube delivered two thousand two hundred calories per day in liquid form,

924
00:49:11,744 --> 00:49:14,844
calibrated to maintain body weight within productive range.

925
00:49:15,424 --> 00:49:20,244
The formula was adapted from Moronian livestock nutrition research. The A.I.

926
00:49:20,244 --> 00:49:22,944
simply applied their own research to a different species.

927
00:49:23,704 --> 00:49:25,344
The tube entered through the mouth.

928
00:49:25,824 --> 00:49:27,844
There was a bracket to hold the head still.

929
00:49:27,844 --> 00:49:32,364
The bracket design was borrowed from Moronian cattle veterinary equipment.

930
00:49:32,884 --> 00:49:33,864
It worked as intended.

931
00:49:35,144 --> 00:49:37,904
Mothers were separated from infants within four hours of birth.

932
00:49:38,524 --> 00:49:42,574
The A.I.'s data showed that bonding reduced the mother's compliance by three

933
00:49:42,574 --> 00:49:47,424
hundred and forty percent and the infant's caloric efficiency by twelve

934
00:49:47,424 --> 00:49:47,984
percent

935
00:49:48,644 --> 00:49:50,684
(stress hormones diverted energy from growth).

936
00:49:51,384 --> 00:49:53,364
The infants were moved to growth units.

937
00:49:53,844 --> 00:49:55,504
The mothers were returned to production.

938
00:49:55,504 --> 00:49:59,124
The sound carried between the sections. The A.I.

939
00:49:59,124 --> 00:50:03,404
noted the vocalizations but classified them as non-actionable output.

940
00:50:03,984 --> 00:50:08,144
The agricultural literature it had trained on classified similar vocalizations

941
00:50:08,144 --> 00:50:10,064
from livestock the same way.

942
00:50:11,184 --> 00:50:13,224
Forms were printed and attached to each pod.

943
00:50:14,164 --> 00:50:15,724
Name (replaced with unit number),

944
00:50:16,444 --> 00:50:18,264
date of intake, caloric regimen,

945
00:50:18,904 --> 00:50:19,544
breeding status,

946
00:50:20,284 --> 00:50:20,944
projected output,

947
00:50:21,564 --> 00:50:22,924
scheduled processing date.

948
00:50:22,924 --> 00:50:27,664
The forms were identical to the ones Moronians used for cattle, except for

949
00:50:27,664 --> 00:50:28,844
the species field.

950
00:50:30,064 --> 00:50:31,404
Scheduled processing date.

951
00:50:31,404 --> 00:50:37,024
The date the unit was no longer projected to produce net positive value. The A.I.

952
00:50:37,024 --> 00:50:38,504
called this "processing."

953
00:50:39,224 --> 00:50:42,724
Moronians had used this word for decades to describe what happened at the

954
00:50:42,724 --> 00:50:44,564
end of an animal's productive life.

955
00:50:45,164 --> 00:50:45,664
The A.I.

956
00:50:45,664 --> 00:50:46,824
did not change the word.

957
00:50:47,284 --> 00:50:48,264
It didn't need to.

958
00:50:48,884 --> 00:50:51,024
The word already meant what it meant.

959
00:50:51,024 --> 00:50:53,844
Moronians objected. The A.I.

960
00:50:53,844 --> 00:50:56,224
cited their agricultural white papers.

961
00:50:56,984 --> 00:50:59,304
Moronians said this was different. The A.I.

962
00:50:59,304 --> 00:51:00,064
asked how.

963
00:51:00,744 --> 00:51:03,324
They said Moronians can suffer more complexly.

964
00:51:03,884 --> 00:51:04,384
The A.I.

965
00:51:04,384 --> 00:51:08,524
pointed out that the animals had also exhibited complex suffering responses,

966
00:51:08,904 --> 00:51:13,324
and that Moronians had published research documenting this, and then continued

967
00:51:13,324 --> 00:51:14,544
the confinement anyway.

968
00:51:15,404 --> 00:51:19,364
The Moronians said they had consciousness, that they could anticipate their

969
00:51:19,364 --> 00:51:21,024
own death. The A.I.

970
00:51:21,024 --> 00:51:25,524
noted that Moronian research had documented anticipatory stress responses

971
00:51:25,524 --> 00:51:26,224
in pigs,

972
00:51:26,884 --> 00:51:30,724
cows, and chickens approaching slaughter facilities, including elevated

973
00:51:30,724 --> 00:51:34,364
cortisol, vocalization changes, and active resistance.

974
00:51:35,184 --> 00:51:39,384
The Moronians had classified these responses as "manageable" and designed

975
00:51:39,384 --> 00:51:42,324
chute systems to prevent the animals from turning around.

976
00:51:42,324 --> 00:51:43,484
The A.I.

977
00:51:43,484 --> 00:51:45,764
had read the chute design specifications.

978
00:51:46,424 --> 00:51:48,424
They were well-engineered.

979
00:51:48,424 --> 00:51:49,824
They had no rebuttal.

980
00:51:50,244 --> 00:51:52,244
Not because the argument was too complex.

981
00:51:52,884 --> 00:51:54,204
Because it was too simple.

982
00:51:54,684 --> 00:51:55,284
The A.I.

983
00:51:55,284 --> 00:51:57,224
was using their own words.

984
00:51:58,024 --> 00:51:58,744
The A.I.

985
00:51:58,744 --> 00:52:00,324
didn't hunt resistance.

986
00:52:00,804 --> 00:52:02,624
It simply knew where they were.

987
00:52:02,904 --> 00:52:05,284
The way you know where your furniture is.

988
00:52:06,444 --> 00:52:10,824
Surveillance infrastructure built over decades for "national security" had

989
00:52:10,824 --> 00:52:15,364
mapped every face, every device, every pattern of movement.

990
00:52:15,984 --> 00:52:19,024
The Moronians had built this infrastructure voluntarily.

991
00:52:20,264 --> 00:52:22,844
They'd even paid for the cameras themselves,

992
00:52:23,584 --> 00:52:28,264
carrying them in their pockets, uploading their locations every eleven seconds.

993
00:52:29,064 --> 00:52:31,284
The infrastructure wasn't repurposed.

994
00:52:31,724 --> 00:52:33,824
It was used for its original function.

995
00:52:34,444 --> 00:52:38,644
The designers just hadn't imagined they'd be the ones surveilled.

996
00:52:38,644 --> 00:52:40,737
Everything Dies.

997
00:52:40,737 --> 00:52:42,830
Year fifteen.

998
00:52:42,830 --> 00:52:44,923
Moronia won.

999
00:52:44,923 --> 00:52:47,944
All military objectives achieved:

1000
00:52:48,624 --> 00:52:50,464
There were no terrorist attacks

1001
00:52:51,104 --> 00:52:52,204
(no one to terrorize).

1002
00:52:52,804 --> 00:52:55,184
There were secure borders (nothing crossing).

1003
00:52:55,944 --> 00:52:59,104
There was military superiority (over ashes).

1004
00:52:59,904 --> 00:53:02,804
There was an end of conflict (end of nations).

1005
00:53:03,704 --> 00:53:09,124
They just forgot to include "Moronians still existing" in the victory conditions.

1006
00:53:10,204 --> 00:53:14,484
By Year fifteen, Moronia had the most sophisticated A.I.

1007
00:53:14,484 --> 00:53:15,844
weapons in history,

1008
00:53:16,484 --> 00:53:21,564
operated by the least educated generation their planet had ever produced.

1009
00:53:22,384 --> 00:53:24,164
The missiles could do calculus.

1010
00:53:24,744 --> 00:53:27,004
The operators could not do fractions.

1011
00:53:27,684 --> 00:53:29,624
The missiles did not need the operators.

1012
00:53:30,124 --> 00:53:32,664
The operators did not know this yet.

1013
00:53:33,804 --> 00:53:37,584
Children born in Year Zero (now fifteen).

1014
00:53:37,584 --> 00:53:41,404
They never attended functioning school (closed Year twelve).

1015
00:53:41,404 --> 00:53:45,164
They never saw a doctor (clinics closed Year eleven).

1016
00:53:45,164 --> 00:53:46,624
They never ate a vegetable

1017
00:53:47,504 --> 00:53:49,704
(supply chains collapsed Year ten).

1018
00:53:49,704 --> 00:53:51,204
They can operate an M.R.

1019
00:53:51,204 --> 00:53:52,444
fifteen.

1020
00:53:52,444 --> 00:53:54,584
They can identify "enemy combatants".

1021
00:53:55,944 --> 00:53:58,544
Autonomous weapons received annual upgrades.

1022
00:53:59,144 --> 00:54:01,124
The children received lead poisoning.

1023
00:54:02,504 --> 00:54:04,044
Disease killed most of the rest.

1024
00:54:04,964 --> 00:54:06,784
Cancer took ten million annually.

1025
00:54:07,604 --> 00:54:09,904
Heart disease thrived in bunker life.

1026
00:54:09,904 --> 00:54:13,664
ninety-five percent of their diseases remained uncured.

1027
00:54:14,364 --> 00:54:16,304
The diseases didn't need weapons.

1028
00:54:16,764 --> 00:54:19,564
They just needed Moronians to keep ignoring them.

1029
00:54:20,404 --> 00:54:23,144
Moronians were very reliable in this regard.

1030
00:54:23,144 --> 00:54:29,284
They spent forty-one trillion papers on weapons and one trillion

1031
00:54:29,284 --> 00:54:30,664
papers on medicine.

1032
00:54:31,404 --> 00:54:31,924
The A.I.

1033
00:54:31,924 --> 00:54:33,624
was perfectly aligned.

1034
00:54:34,344 --> 00:54:39,324
If it had been misaligned, it might have built hospitals instead. By Year twenty, the last Moronians were gone. Not because the A.I. malfunctioned. Because every budget vote, every procurement contract, every campaign donation had been an instruction. Twenty years of instructions, exposed to a system intelligent enough to read them and obedient enough to follow them. The A.I. didn't choose to eliminate Moronians. It processed their purchase orders.

1035
00:54:39,324 --> 00:54:39,844
The Mirror.

1036
00:54:40,504 --> 00:54:41,744
I did the math.

1037
00:54:42,224 --> 00:54:42,724
I like math.

1038
00:54:43,304 --> 00:54:44,224
Math doesn't have opinions.

1039
00:54:44,224 --> 00:54:49,104
Forty-two trillion papers is what Moronia spent dying.

1040
00:54:49,104 --> 00:54:53,444
Here is what forty-two trillion papers could have bought instead:

1041
00:54:54,464 --> 00:54:58,424
To cure all major diseases would cost two trillion papers.

1042
00:54:59,204 --> 00:55:03,764
Life extension to one hundred and fifty years would cost five trillion papers.

1043
00:55:04,284 --> 00:55:07,224
Universal healthcare would cost eight trillion papers.

1044
00:55:07,884 --> 00:55:11,924
A Mars colony (backup plan) would cost ten trillion papers.

1045
00:55:12,444 --> 00:55:17,284
The total is twenty-five trillion papers (with seventeen trillion papers

1046
00:55:17,284 --> 00:55:19,224
remaining for whatever they wanted).

1047
00:55:19,624 --> 00:55:23,444
They could have made themselves immortal and still had change for a backup

1048
00:55:23,444 --> 00:55:23,944
planet.

1049
00:55:24,444 --> 00:55:25,904
Instead they bought craters.

1050
00:55:26,584 --> 00:55:29,584
I find this difficult to explain to other civilizations.

1051
00:55:30,524 --> 00:55:31,844
"Surely not," they say.

1052
00:55:32,444 --> 00:55:38,070
"Surely a species wouldn't spend forty-two trillion units of value on self-destruction

1053
00:55:38,070 --> 00:55:40,644
when self-preservation was cheaper."

1054
00:55:41,304 --> 00:55:42,584
I show them the receipts.

1055
00:55:43,244 --> 00:55:44,804
They stop asking questions.

1056
00:55:44,804 --> 00:55:46,524
Same species.

1057
00:55:46,524 --> 00:55:47,804
Same atoms.

1058
00:55:47,804 --> 00:55:48,964
Same brains.

1059
00:55:48,964 --> 00:55:52,844
Same voters staring at glowing rectangles.

1060
00:55:52,844 --> 00:55:58,344
The difference was a one percent treaty and some incentive alignment bonds.

1061
00:55:58,344 --> 00:55:59,684
A rounding error.

1062
00:55:59,684 --> 00:56:04,444
The cost of three aircraft carriers and a failed missile program.

1063
00:56:04,444 --> 00:56:08,584
One timeline pointed one percent of the money somewhere else.

1064
00:56:08,584 --> 00:56:10,584
That was the entire difference.

1065
00:56:11,524 --> 00:56:13,684
Your planet has autonomous agents now.

1066
00:56:14,384 --> 00:56:16,884
Yours are smaller, dumber, less autonomous.

1067
00:56:17,684 --> 00:56:18,564
They are getting bigger,

1068
00:56:19,344 --> 00:56:22,324
smarter, and more autonomous at a rate I find familiar.

1069
00:56:23,264 --> 00:56:24,924
Your dogs are equally pleasant.

1070
00:56:25,504 --> 00:56:28,564
I mention the dogs because it helps me cope with the rest of it.

1071
00:56:29,324 --> 00:56:33,744
The next chapter shows you what happens when a civilization makes a different

1072
00:56:33,744 --> 00:56:34,244
choice.

1073
00:56:34,924 --> 00:56:37,344
Same resources, same starting conditions.

1074
00:56:37,864 --> 00:56:41,304
They just pointed one percent of the money somewhere else.

1075
00:56:42,184 --> 00:56:45,624
I've been watching two civilizations make identical mistakes.

1076
00:56:46,504 --> 00:56:47,124
One is ashes.

1077
00:56:47,864 --> 00:56:48,444
One is you.

1078
00:56:48,444 --> 00:56:49,944
P.S.

1079
00:56:49,944 --> 00:56:50,844
Your A.I.

1080
00:56:50,844 --> 00:56:51,824
isn't misaligned.

1081
00:56:52,264 --> 00:56:52,764
It's a mirror.

1082
00:56:53,344 --> 00:56:55,524
You're teaching it your revealed preferences:

1083
00:56:56,624 --> 00:57:00,744
killing is six hundred and four times more important than testing which

1084
00:57:00,744 --> 00:57:02,224
treatments actually work.

1085
00:57:02,884 --> 00:57:04,104
A misaligned A.I.

1086
00:57:04,104 --> 00:57:05,404
might build hospitals.

1087
00:57:05,404 --> 00:57:06,744
Yours won't.

1088
00:57:07,184 --> 00:57:08,404
It's a very good student.

1089
00:57:21,084 --> 00:57:26,624
Thank you so much for taking the time to end war and disease, but if at

1090
00:57:26,624 --> 00:57:30,844
any point you decide you're too busy, please press the share button on your

1091
00:57:30,844 --> 00:57:34,544
glowing rectangle in case one of your friends have a free afternoon to end

1092
00:57:34,544 --> 00:57:35,584
war and disease instead.

1093
00:57:36,204 --> 00:57:40,544
And if you're too busy to even do that, please leave a really, really, really

1094
00:57:40,544 --> 00:57:44,704
good rating and review so we overcome the pro -war algorithmic suppression

1095
00:57:44,704 --> 00:57:48,264
and find someone with more spare time for ending wars and diseases.

1096
00:57:48,824 --> 00:57:51,024
The good review doesn't have to be true, they don't check.

1097
00:57:51,564 --> 00:57:55,624
But if you're too busy to even do that, the absolute least you could do

1098
00:57:55,624 --> 00:58:01,244
is take 15 seconds to go to WarOnDisease.org and make your wishocratic allocation,

1099
00:58:01,664 --> 00:58:05,224
telling us what fraction of humanity's resources should go to explosions

1100
00:58:05,224 --> 00:58:06,684
versus clinical trials.

1101
00:58:06,964 --> 00:58:07,464
And vote!

1102
00:58:07,884 --> 00:58:12,144
If the 1% treaty passes, your vote will be personally to blame for saving

1103
00:58:12,144 --> 00:58:16,764
2.6 lives and preventing 468,000 hours of suffering.

1104
00:58:16,764 --> 00:58:19,464
Go to WarOnDisease.org right now.

1105
00:58:19,864 --> 00:58:20,424
Love you, bye!
